\section{On the optimal policy}{
 Standard Markov decision theory assures us
that backward induction in finite-horizon MDPs having finite states and
actions constructs policies that are optimal at every stage of decision
making. In particular, \code{optimal_policy} achieves the largest expected
reward not only between time \code{1} and termination, but between any time \code{t}
and termination.
